WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.710
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.570
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.100
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.100
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.430
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.430
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.410
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.920
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:40.200
Evacuate into the building! Hurry!

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:17.580
Episode 33

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:17.580
The Puzzle of Project Shadow

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:34.340
Altogether now!

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:40.930
Where's that sound coming from?

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:47.680
Over there.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.780
Wait! I can still use that, so put it over here.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:08.580
Everyone, let's carry the rescue supplies to the cafeteria.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.250
Right!

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:11.370
Chris!

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.420
I brought a lot of food.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:17.710
Dad?

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.560
This is hard work.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:33.900
Of course.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.690
After all, you did carry the heaviest box.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.400
Is that supposed to be sarcasm?

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.990
Still nothing?

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.530
Have you found our son yet?

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.870
Is this your child?

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.120
Mommy!

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.210
Jim! Thank goodness!

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.090
Sonic, thank you!

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.340
Thank you very much!

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:10.100
When I was a child, I imagined that the President was a superhero that led the way and stood up against evil.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:15.310
Just like Sonic.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:16.360
Next.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:20.070
This bill is a tax cut for citizens in disaster-stricken areas.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.950
But in reality, this is what the President does.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:28.200
This bill is for the government to pay the loans for destroyed residential buildings.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:31.660
All I do is sign papers everyday.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.540
Special budget increase for GUN

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:40.300
I'm nothing like a superhero.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:44.840
This includes the plan for the mass production of new robot models.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.050
Okay.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.640
Is this it?

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:52.180
What's this?

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:56.810
He's the driver for the President's mobile office.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.650
His driving techniques in emergency situations are impeccable.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.240
Take care, Chris.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.030
Uhh, Mom...

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:11.660
It's sad that they have to part.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.710
They're making such a big deal out of nothing.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:20.800
Yeah. They're only going to be apart for a month or two until we get settled.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.380
Call me when you get there.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.970
Promise!

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.010
Sure thing.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:31.390
It's going to get lonely with both Chris and Mr. Stewart gone.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:32.930
Yeah.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:41.110
Just when I was getting used to everything...

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.910
Huh? Where's Sonic?

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.990
He's busy.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:53.410
Oh yeah. He told me to tell you, "See you later."

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:55.370
Oh.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:57.540
Come on, Chris.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:02.000
The distance between here and the city is just a single flight on X-Tornado.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:05.760
And Sonic can get here in an instant.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:07.680
I know, but...

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:14.180
Even if Sonic went to the city with you, he's not the type who would settle down there.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:15.600
That's true.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.640
Take care!

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:21.520
See you all again!

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:40.460
We can compete against Eggman's robots with these.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:44.420
Yeah, we won't let Dr. Eggman push us around anymore.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.220
How dare they act so arrogant!

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:53.300
All they did was copy my robots!

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:56.470
But should we underestimate them?

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:59.390
If they come as a large army, it'll be dangerous.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:01.520
I know!

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:06.690
I'll hack GUN's main computer and find out their situation.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:15.700
This is nothing.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:19.710
Let's see...

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.840
They've made many varieties.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.340
What?

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:37.770
What's the matter?

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.480
Dr. Eggman?

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:47.650
I was born in this world.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:53.820
The genius scientist Professor Gerald Robotnik!

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:55.820
He's my grandfather.

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:59.750
That means this world and our world...

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.580
How are they related?

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:09.670
A completely different world that shares the same time and space... In other words, it's a parallel dimension.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:15.260
Why is my grandfather's name in GUN's database?

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.510
Another password?

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:21.140
Damn!

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:29.820
Damn! It's no good!

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.910
Maria.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:37.700
Can it be?

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.450
M-A-R-I-A

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.120
You gained access!

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:47.250
What's wrong?

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:55.130
A hacker got the password for the special file that no one has been able to open for the past 50 years. He's hacking our system!

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:55.970
What?

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:56.970
You mean that special file?

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:58.930
They found us!

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:00.930
Hurry!

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:04.640
I know! Downloading file!

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.060
Deleting original file.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:09.690
Hurry up and shut down the computer!

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:11.230
I'm doing that right now!

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.110
Download...

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:17.610
Completed!

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:19.950
Original file deleted!

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:23.410
That was close.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:26.670
What?

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:29.380
This is...

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:31.460
Grandfather's diary!

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:38.340
I have finally finished creating the ultimate creature, Shadow.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:40.800
I also completely control his memories.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:43.930
I leave everything to Shadow.

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:48.150
If anyone wishes for power, then awaken him...

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:52.360
...if you desire to bring despair to the world.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:55.780
The ultimate creature Shadow?

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:58.200
Project Shadow?

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:03.410
Please don't ask me what it's about, Miss Rouge.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:05.620
Because we don't know either.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.580
What do you mean?

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:19.470
All the records of this project were deliberately destroyed 50 years ago by the 13th President before me.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:24.520
But there was one copy that wasn't erased and left in GUN's database.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:27.230
To put it more accurately, it couldn't be erased.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:31.520
Without a password, it couldn't be deleted nor opened.

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:34.480
And Dr. Eggman hacked it.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:36.740
That's right.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.660
So what's our mission?

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.780
To investigate Project Shadow?

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:47.040
No. We'll appoint someone else to do that.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:52.960
We'd like you to investigate what Dr. Eggman is up to.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:54.130
Okay.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:58.300
Vanishing Commando, stop the car.

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:00.800
That was my name until yesterday.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:03.550
Today, I'm "Headlights of Goodbye Youth".

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.520
Now what should we do?

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:13.020
How about an undercover investigation?

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:16.320
How daring. But I think it's a good idea.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:20.320
That means we need bait.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:22.660
Bait that will hook our prey.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.650
Chris, good morning!

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:02.860
Yeah... Good morning...

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:05.160
What's the matter?

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:07.240
Well...

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:10.000
You'll get used to it in time.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.660
I guess so.

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:28.470
What's wrong, Chris?

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:31.230
Well...

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:35.730
It takes time to get used to a new environment.

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:38.480
It was the same for me when I was young.

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:41.570
Think of it as another experience.

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:49.370
Think of it like this - Chaos Control sent Sonic and his friends to this world, and they can't return home.

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:53.000
But they're doing the best they can.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:14.270
You're right. I forgot about that.

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.350
I have to follow their example.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:17.770
Right.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:24.860
Where are you?

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:27.700
I'm scared!

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:29.620
Over there.

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:31.200
I'll save you right away!

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:37.080
Are you all right?

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:39.670
Yes, I'm fine.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:46.760
It's you!

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:52.010
How dare you, Sonic!

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:54.930
How dare you save me when I didn't ask you to!

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:56.810
Sorry about that.

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.100
Later.

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:01.230
W-Wait!

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:02.770
What?

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:08.030
I'm not going to say, "Thank you for saving me!"

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.990
Then don't say it.

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:13.450
So don't you dare say, "You're welcome", either!

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:17.410
If you do, you're gonna get it! Understand?

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:20.710
Okay, fine. Bye.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:25.550
Stupid, stupid, stupid Sonic!

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:29.890
Oh, umm...

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.350
If no one's going to use it...

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.060
Stupid!

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:37.140
I'm sorry!

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:47.190
Isn't it true that all you actually want to do is look for jewels?

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:54.450
How rude. Like I said, if you want to hook Eggman, we have to bring him a Chaos Emerald.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:00.960
Are you sure we're going in the right direction?

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:08.420
We're close.

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:19.390
I am Scarlet Garcia from Station Square.

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:21.270
It's nice to meet you.

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:23.900
Oh, so it's you.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:27.230
I watched your report on Perfect Chaos.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:28.900
That must have been tough.

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:30.900
Yes.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.330
Looks like everyone watched the program.

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:40.080
It's harder to find those who haven't.

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:47.960
Franklin, you're already here?

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:49.630
Yes.

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.220
Let me introduce you.

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:53.010
Okay.

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:56.390
This is Franklin the director.

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:58.970
Nice to meet you. I'm Scarlet Garcia.

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:03.020
It's an honor to meet you, Miss Garcia.

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:08.320
The Secret of The Project Shadow.

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.360
Are you serious?

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:13.410
Yes. Are you interested?

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:15.700
Yes, but...

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:22.370
Your journalist father was pursuing this story right before he passed away.

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:24.830
To put it bluntly, this is dangerous.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:26.670
I know.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:31.130
There are people who don't want anyone to find out about Project Shadow.

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:33.510
A shadow organization that even the government doesn't know about.

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:34.380
Then why?

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.720
Because I still want to know!

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:39.350
As a journalist, don't you also want to know?

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:42.060
Personally, as Scarlet Garcia?

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:48.770
I promise to risk my life to guarantee your safety.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:51.900
So want to do this together?

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:02.450
It's not a Chaos Emerald, but...

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:05.330
It's so heavy!

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:07.040
Stop!

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:10.000
Give me back the Master Emerald!

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:16.840
I won't let you get away!

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:24.640
Rouge!

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:29.940
Ouch...

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:31.650
Rouge!

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:34.950
I found a Chaos Emerald!

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:38.950
But I'm also taking this!

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:40.910
Hey you!

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:44.290
This happens because you want the bigger one.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:48.960
I don't know who you are, but do you realize what you're doing?

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:55.630
That Master Emerald has the important role of preventing the Chaos Emeralds from going out of control!

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:58.220
Hey! Are you listening to me?

00:17:58.220 --> 00:18:00.010
No, I'm not.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:02.350
Why you!

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.560
How's that?

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:12.190
A woman?

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:18.490
Oh no!

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:25.500
What was that?

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:37.550
An intruder entered through the front of Gate #3.

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:42.550
The enemy is currently heading towards the basement of North Area Headquarters.

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:48.690
All members on standby, prepare for battle immediately.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:51.980
All those on site, intercept using the normal procedure.

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:54.610
Prevent the enemy from infiltrating the classified area.

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:56.480
This is not a drill.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:59.400
I repeat, this is not a drill!

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:08.580
They're all talk.

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:21.590
Now let me take a look at GUN's super-confidential weapon that my grandfather created.

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:23.760
Wait, Dr. Eggman!

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:27.810
We're coming too!

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:33.770
But you're useless.

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:38.110
Dr. Eggman, you don't have to be so cold.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:39.940
Yeah!

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:52.290
Oh no!

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.170
A Laser Hunter?

00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:58.630
Click.

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:03.800
How annoying!

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:13.190
I even blew up the door!

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:14.980
What?

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:19.320
Dr. Eggman is on Prison Island.

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:29.040
What are you doing?

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:29.950
Let's go!

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:34.170
Wait, Dr. Eggman!

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:47.180
Dr. Eggman, are you sure it's here?

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:50.680
There's no mistake! It's definitely in the back.

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:15.000
That was easy.

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:29.140
All clear.

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:32.390
Now, Dr. Eggman.

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:35.770
At least you guys are dressed appropriately.

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:44.490
It's smaller than I expected.

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:49.990
After registering the user data, I enter the password.

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:52.740
M-A-R-I-A.

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:56.040
And finally, I place the Chaos Emerald.

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:36.330
What? You're...!

00:22:45.090 --> 00:22:54.510
<b>Watashitachi no sekai wa mahou o kakerarete</b>

00:22:45.090 --> 00:22:54.510
<i>There’s magic cast on our world.</i>

00:22:54.510 --> 00:23:03.480
<b>Ai suru to kime kisae namida ni ujirareteru</b>

00:22:54.510 --> 00:23:03.480
<i>The nervousness of love is sealed by tears.</i>

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:12.370
<b>Boy boy futari de jumon wo sagashi ni ikou</b>

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:12.370
<i>Boy, let’s search for a spell together,</i>

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:21.960
<b>Kinji rareta yume wo kanaerareru kuni he</b>

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:21.960
<i>To a land where our forbidden dreams can come true.</i>

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:30.930
<b>Dare ni mo naisho de ashita na tchi awaseshiyou</b>

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:30.930
<i>Let’s secretly meet tomorrow.</i>

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:41.100
<b>Itsuka kotori wo ume ta yowake no mieru oka de</b>

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:41.100
<i>At the place where we buried the bird, the hill where we can see the sunrise.</i>

00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:49.860
<b>Tsumetai asamoya kimi to te wo tsunaidara</b>

00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:49.860
<i>In the cold morning mist, if I hold hands with you.</i>

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:59.040
<b>Hikaru michi no fuuin ga tokeru yo</b>

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:59.040
<i>The seal to the shining path will be broken.</i>

00:23:59.560 --> 00:24:03.880
<b>Hateshinaku</b>

00:23:59.560 --> 00:24:03.880
<i>Forever...</i>

00:24:30.760 --> 00:25:35.430
Sonic the Fugitive
